maria (DevEx): Heads-up — found a reproducible deadlock in the sample paginator that happens when an auth refresh coincides with 429s + client-side retries. UI stays loading and we burn through quota. Repro steps in under a minute.

maria (DevEx): Repro:
1) Use quickstart sample with pageSize=50 and concurrency 4
2) Force token expiry (short-lived token) and trigger load of many pages
3) Server returns 429 on some requests during token refresh
4) Client retries whole page instead of single request => duplicate inflight requests => quota blowout and spinner never resolves

maria (DevEx): Logs:
```
[2026-03-20T16:02:03Z] GET /v1/items?page=3 -> 200 ok
[2026-03-20T16:02:04Z] GET /v1/items?page=4 -> 429 rate_limit
[2026-03-20T16:02:04Z] token refresh started
[2026-03-20T16:02:04Z] retrying page 4 (attempt 1)
[2026-03-20T16:02:05Z] GET /v1/items?page=4 -> 429 rate_limit
[2026-03-20T16:02:05Z] retrying page 4 (attempt 2)
[2026-03-20T16:02:05Z] GET /v1/items?page=4 -> 200 ok  <-- duplicated work
```

sam (SDK): Oof. Can you paste the retry config from the sample app? I want to see whether we're re-running the whole page fetch loop or individual HTTP calls.

maria (DevEx): sample code from sdk-paginator.js: 
```
async function fetchPage(p) {
  for (let i=0;i<3;i++) {
    try {
      let res = await api.listItems({page:p});
      return res;
    } catch (e) {
      if (e.code === 'UNAUTH' ) { await auth.refresh(); continue; }
      if (e.code === 'RATE_LIMIT') { await sleep(1000 * Math.pow(2,i)); continue; }
      throw e;
    }
  }
  throw new Error('page failed');
}
```

leo (Platform): I think the logic retries the whole page (outer loop) and `auth.refresh()` is racing with other inflight requests that also retry — so when token rotates we end up sending multiple retries for the same page. Also no concurrency cap per paginator.

alex (Eng): Root cause summary: retry loop lives at page-level instead of per-request, and we don't attach a request-level idempotency key or a per-page concurrency guard. Combined with unlimited client concurrency this makes duplicate requests amplify when 429s and refreshes happen.

sam (SDK): Proposed short-term mitigations:
- move retry to the HTTP wrapper (request-level), not the page-level loop
- when auth refresh happens, block new outgoing retries until refresh completes (small critical section)
- add jitter + cap retries to avoid stampede

alex (Eng): Patch idea (pseudo):
```
// http-wrapper
async function requestWithRetry(req) {
  const key = req.idempotencyKey || generateKey(req);
  for (let att=0; att < MAX_ATT; att++) {
    if (isRefreshingToken()) { await waitForRefresh(); }
    let r = await send(req);
    if (r.status === 200) return r;
    if (r.status === 429) { await sleep(backoff(att)); continue; }
    throw r;
  }
}
```

devsk: I can run integration tests against the quickstart app with a short token to verify. Also can add an in-memory per-page mutex to avoid duplicate inflight page fetches.

ratebot: [event] rate_limit bucket=user:client hit 112 times in 2m (sample-app)

ci-bot: heads-up — one flaky test `paginator/integration.test.js` failed twice on main in the last 6 hours, reproduces locally with token TTL=1s

sam (SDK): Also consider preserving `nextPageToken` semantics: retries should request the same cursor; don't re-run pages that have already been fully consumed. Idempotency + cursor check prevents double-processing.

maria (DevEx): UX ask: if a page ultimately fails, surface a single page-level error in the UI (not an infinite spinner). Also add a small retry counter and a "Try again" CTA.

alex (Eng): I'll open a PR implementing request-level retries + per-page mutex + jittered backoff. Will also add an optional `maxConcurrentPages` config in sample app. PR: #5432 (WIP).

devsk: Ran quick local loopback with the changes — can't reproduce the spinner anymore. Confirmed rate_limit events drop from ~100 to <10 in 2m.

maria (DevEx): Awesome, can you add a short blurb in the quickstart README explaining the concurrency knob and the auth edge-case? New users kept hitting this and it's a big onboarding pain.

alex (Eng): Will do. Also adding a small test that simulates concurrent refresh + 429 to prevent regressions.

sam (SDK): Follow-ups: add idempotency headers in HTTP client and expose `retryPolicy` in SDK config. I'll draft docs.

maria (DevEx): Thanks all — great quick turnaround. Leaving this thread as the repro record. :thumbsup:
